{
  "repo": "microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat",
  "number": 5992,
  "title": "Fix feedback activities dropping custom properties of the bot's VoteAction",
  "body": "> Feedback activities drop the custom properties of the bot's like, dislike and vote actions, so bots cannot match feedback to the answer. Test from #5986 by @ahonamatata.\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed feedback activities dropping custom properties of the bot's like, dislike and vote actions, in PR [#5992](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/5992), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n## Description\n\nSince 4.19.0, the feedback event sends the action after Schema.org parsing, which drops unknown properties and turns values into arrays, and the form's invoke sends no entity. Both now send the action as the bot sent it, as 4.18.2 did, with `actionStatus: \"CompletedActionStatus\"`.\n\n## Design\n\n- Looked up by `@type` in the raw message entity, then the `VoteAction` by `actionOption`, as `channelData.feedbackLoop` replaces the bot's entities.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `getOriginalActionEntity.ts`: finds the bot's own action\n- `ActivityFeedbackComposer.tsx`: sends it with the invoke and the event\n- `feedback.compatibility.potentialAction.html`: like then dislike with custom properties, snapshots 1–3\n- `feedback.compatibility.{noReview,review}.html`: #5986's test split in two, user prompt first (`ClientCapabilities` goes on the first outgoing activity)\n- `feedbackActivityStatus.click.html`: `@type` back to `\"VoteAction\"`\n\n- [x] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [x] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [ ] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [x] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n",
